  "result": "I made three fixes:\n\n- **Switching off now sticks:** `src/server/repositories/webhook-repository.ts:58` only saved the on/off setting when it was on, so switching off was silently dropped. It now saves `false` as well. The code that queues new events already skips endpoints that are off, so nothing new is queued for them now.\n- **Queued events for off endpoints fail:** in `src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts:63`, the delivery run now marks a queued delivery failed if its endpoint is switched off, not only if the endpoint is gone. It counts as failed, and endpoints that are on are delivered as before.\n- **Off endpoints still count toward the plan:** `createWebhook` in `src/server/services/webhook-service.ts` now counts every endpoint with `countEndpoints`, whether it's on or off. A workspace at its limit can't get another endpoint by switching one off.\n\nI haven't run the tests.",
